 "result": "Start with these spots in `src/tessel/`:\n\n- **`app.py:364-409`**: `static_cache_seconds(filename)` sets the `max_age` for static files, and the static-file view (`app.py:407`) passes it to `send_file`. The default is `None`, which means `no-cache` with conditional (ETag) requests, so browsers revalidate rather than reuse stale files blindly.\n- **`bundles.py:56-101`**: the same logic for bundle static folders. Check whether a bundle overrides it.\n- **`helpers.py:405-406`**: the fallback to `ctx.app.static_cache_seconds` when `max_age` isn't passed, plus the `send_file` docs on `conditional`, `etag` and `max_age` (~lines 422-480).\n\nAlso check:\n\n- **Overrides**: grep your own app code for a `static_cache_seconds` override or a configured value, since a long `max_age` there would explain stale CSS.\n- **Front server or CDN**: any nginx/CDN `Cache-Control` or `expires` rules sit outside this code and can override it.\n- **Filenames**: if the CSS filenames don't change per deploy (no hash or `?v=`), a long cache will serve the old file.",
